### Opt-in to avoiding a `NavigationException` during static server-side rendering with `NavigationManager.NavigateTo`

Calling [NavigationManager.NavigateTo](/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.aspnetcore.components.navigationmanager.navigateto) during static server-side rendering (static SSR) throws a [NavigationException](/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.aspnetcore.components.navigationexception), interrupting execution before being converted to a redirection response. This can cause confusion during debugging and is inconsistent with interactive rendering behavior, where code after [NavigateTo](/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.aspnetcore.components.navigationmanager.navigateto) continues to execute normally.

In .NET 10, you can set the `<BlazorDisableThrowNavigationException>` MSBuild property to `true` in the app's project file in order to avoid throwing the exception during static SSR:

```
<PropertyGroup>
  <BlazorDisableThrowNavigationException>true</BlazorDisableThrowNavigationException>
</PropertyGroup>
```

With the MSBuild property set, calling [NavigationManager.NavigateTo](/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.aspnetcore.components.navigationmanager.navigateto) during static SSR no longer throws a [NavigationException](/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.aspnetcore.components.navigationexception). Instead, it behaves consistently with interactive rendering by performing the navigation without throwing an exception. Code after [NavigationManager.NavigateTo](/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.aspnetcore.components.navigationmanager.navigateto) executes before the redirection occurs.

The .NET 10 Blazor Web App project template sets the MSBuild property to `true` by default. We recommend that apps updating to .NET 10 use the new MSBuild property and avoid the prior behavior.

If the MSBuild property is used, code that relied on [NavigationException](/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.aspnetcore.components.navigationexception) being thrown should be updated. In the default Blazor Identity UI of the Blazor Web App project template before the release of .NET 10, the `IdentityRedirectManager` throws an [InvalidOperationException](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.invalidoperationexception) after calling `RedirectTo` to ensure that the method wasn't invoked during interactive rendering. This exception and the [`[DoesNotReturn]` attributes](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.diagnostics.codeanalysis.doesnotreturnattribute) should now be removed when the MSBuild property is used. For more information, see [Migrate from ASP.NET Core in .NET 9 to ASP.NET Core in .NET 10](../migration/90-to-100?view=aspnetcore-10.0#when-navigation-errors-are-disabled-in-a-blazor-web-app-with-individual-accounts).

### Blazor router has a `NotFoundPage` parameter

